# Synthetic credentials for the isolated local Compose fixture only.
API_RUNTIME=local
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://foundation_local:local_fixture_only@127.0.0.1:55432/foundation_local
API_HOST=127.0.0.1
API_PORT=3001
BROWSER_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Hosted API: do not copy the local binding or synthetic URL above to Vercel.
# Set API_RUNTIME=vercel there; VERCEL and PORT are platform-managed.
# Replace each bracketed value privately with approved Connect Session metadata.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<role>.<project-ref>:<percent-encoded-password>@<exact-session-host>:5432/<database>
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=<20-letter-project-ref>
# SUPABASE_SESSION_HOST=<exact-aws-session-host-from-Connect>
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_NAME=<database-from-Connect>
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_USER=<role>.<project-ref>
# BROWSER_ORIGIN=https://<approved-browser-host>
# Optional only when the verified chain needs a custom root: actual CA PEM,
# not a path or literal backslash-n string. System trusted roots are used if omitted.
# DATABASE_CA_PEM="-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
# <verified-CA-certificate-body>
# -----END CERTIFICATE-----"
#
# Separately authorized operator environment; never set these in the API function.
# MIGRATION_TARGET=supabase
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<approved-role>.<project-ref>:<percent-encoded-password>@<exact-session-host>:5432/<database>
# MIGRATION_CONFIRM_PROJECT_REF=<same-approved-project-ref>
# Uses the same SUPABASE_* target tuple and optional DATABASE_CA_PEM.
# Neither a Supabase management token nor Vercel project/token IDs are API runtime inputs.

# Supabase-local development alternative (synthetic, after supabase:start):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# Use explicit process configuration; do not overwrite an existing .env.
# Gateway/Studio are disabled in the minimum DB-only local stack.
#
# Selected Vercel Production runtime (not a local profile or deployment proof):
# API_RUNTIME=vercel
# VERCEL=1 and PORT are platform-managed; never copy them into local profiles.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=eotmpaliqcxxcotrcols
# SUPABASE_SESSION_HOST=aws-0-ap-northeast-2.pooler.supabase.com
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_NAME=postgres
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_USER=postgres.eotmpaliqcxxcotrcols
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.eotmpaliqcxxcotrcols:<encoded-owner-password>@aws-0-ap-northeast-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
# PREVIEW_ACCESS_KEY=<separate-owner-generated-64-lowercase-hex-key>
# BROWSER_ORIGIN=https://app.lovora.us
# PREVIEW_ACCESS_KEY protects every non-preflight request, including health endpoints.
# Never include API_HOST/API_PORT, MIGRATION_*, operator credentials or Vercel tokens.

# App foundation is opt-in. Do not enable on production before the separately
# approved Auth/role/retention setup and schema-changing release integration.
# APP_SCHEMA_MODE=strict
# The separately approved bridge uses APP_SCHEMA_MODE=activation-bridge and
# APP_FOUNDATION_ENABLED=false explicitly. Only exact OLD or TARGET history is
# ready; no app routes are mounted. Local bridge also requires PREVIEW_ACCESS_KEY.
# Activation configuration workers set APP_ACTIVATION_CONFIG_DIGEST to the
# approved SHA-256 of the canonical phase runtime string map. Startup recomputes
# it; protected health responses attest it, while denied requests disclose none.
# Do not invent a digest, include platform metadata, or use this value as a secret.
# APP_FOUNDATION_ENABLED=true
# APP_WORKSPACE_ID=<explicitly-bootstrapped-workspace-uuid>
# APP_AUTH_URL=https://<approved-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1
# APP_AUTH_API_KEY=<publishable-or-matching-project-legacy-anon-key>
# APP_EMAIL_ENABLED=false
# APP_RETENTION_POLICY_ID=<approved-retention-policy-identifier>
# When real invitation delivery is approved, set APP_EMAIL_ENABLED=true and:
# APP_AUTH_ADMIN_KEY=<separate-server-only-Auth-admin-key>
# No admin key is accepted while delivery is disabled. No HS256 JWT fallback.
# App runtime DB identity must be app_runtime locally or app_runtime.<project-ref>
# for the unchanged reviewed hosted Session endpoint; never use postgres for app mode.
# New app routes require X-App-Access-Token in addition to the technical bearer.
# App-enabled local mode also requires PREVIEW_ACCESS_KEY; use only explicitly
# approved loopback fixtures. Auth callback UI/BFF is a separate FE deliverable.
#
# Separate explicit operator process only; never copy APP_OPERATOR_* into Vercel:
# APP_OPERATOR_TARGET=local
# APP_OPERATOR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app_operator:<synthetic-or-approved-password>@127.0.0.1:<approved-port>/<approved-database>
# APP_OPERATOR_AUTH_KEY=<separate-operator-Auth-admin-key>
# APP_OPERATOR_CONFIRM_WORKSPACE=<same-APP_WORKSPACE_ID>
# APP_OPERATOR_APPROVAL_ID=<recorded-approval-uuid>
# APP_OPERATOR_USER_ID=<verified-Auth-user-uuid>
# APP_OPERATOR_PROFILE_NAME=<approved-display-name>
# APP_OPERATOR_WORKSPACE_NAME=<approved-workspace-name>
# Hosted operator also needs APP_OPERATOR_TARGET=supabase, the reviewed
# SUPABASE_* tuple with app_operator.<project-ref>, and
# APP_OPERATOR_CONFIRM_PROJECT_REF=<same-approved-project-ref>.
# Unknown delivery reconciliation additionally requires its exact invitation ID,
# outcome confirmed|failed, and APP_OPERATOR_CONFIRM_PROVIDER_EVIDENCE equal to
# the recorded approval UUID. This is never an automatic retry or public endpoint.
#
# Separate role-provisioning process, before app migrations; never API runtime:
# APP_ROLES_APPROVAL_ID=<recorded-role-approval-uuid>
# APP_ROLES_CONFIRM_TARGET=supabase:<same-approved-project-ref>
# APP_ROLES_RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL=<same-target-session-url-for-app_runtime>
# APP_ROLES_OPERATOR_DATABASE_URL=<same-target-session-url-for-app_operator>
# Use the independent MIGRATION_* authority above, not app_operator for DDL.
# Existing roles must match exactly; no automatic password, grant or role repair.
